", "artifact_type": "regulatory", "relevance_note": "Highlights the need for repeatability, reliability, and performance of electronic programmable systems."}, {"artifact_id": "qmsr-820.35-records", "artifact_type": "regulatory", "relevance_note": "Requires records of complaint review, evaluation, and investigation."}, {"artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2026A", "artifact_type": "test_log", "relevance_note": "Provides data related to the missed ventricular tachycardia episode; confirms details of the event."}], "missing_evidence": [], "rationale": "The reported incident involves a failure to detect a clinically significant ventricular tachycardia episode, which represents a serious potential patient-safety risk even though the event self-resolved with no recorded adverse outcome. This requires investigation under EU MDR Article 10(9) and 21 CFR \u00a7 820.35 regarding complaint handling and record maintenance. The device's failure to flag this episode may indicate an issue with its performance in line with intended use, as outlined in EU MDR Annex I Section 17.1 concerning electronic programmable systems. While no immediate field safety action is indicated given the self-resolved nature of the event and lack of recurrence, a thorough investigation is necessary to determine the root cause and prevent future occurrences.", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 3}, "final_report_sha256": "b04672197bf5251b2077ea0f6a97d9538ecdf932c41dc49fa29f67a0618e8be7", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 0, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": [], "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0025", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 0, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0025_r2", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0025", "schema_version": "2.1.0", "severity": 3, "shacl_findings": [], "state_terminal": "terminal", "termination_reason": "advisory_complete", "timestamp_utc": "2026-08-04T23:48:03.34